            "title": "South Korea online retailer Coupang faces US securities class action over massive data breach",
            "description": "",
            "summary": "South Korean e-commerce company Coupang  has been sued in a U.S. court in an investor class action \u200balleging violations of securities laws after a cybersecurity breach exposed \u200cpersonal information of more than 33 million customers.  The lawsuit, filed last week in federal court in \u200cCalifornia, claims Coupang, its CEO and Chairman Bom Kim and its Chief Financial Officer Gaurav Anand misled investors about the company\u2019s data security practices and failed to disclose the breach in a timely way.  The company, dubbed the Amazon.com of South Korea, previously said it would tighten security to prevent another data leak.",
